---
/**
 * /guides/skill-changes - class-by-class rundown of first-job skill
 * kit differences from v83 to CoT 2.
 *
 * SEO target: 'maplestory classic worlds skill changes v83',
 * 'MSCW new skills', 'MSCW Bowman Blessing of Amazon removed',
 * 'maplestory classic warrior new passive'. Returning-player
 * query intent.
 *
 * All change claims below are verified against the CoT 2 client
 * datamine (via osmsdataexplorer.com's skill dump). Numeric values
 * (damage %, max levels, MP costs) still reflect v83-era baseline
 * pending live-server verification during Founder's Access. The
 * job MDs (src/content/jobs/*.md) are the source of truth for the
 * skill lists cited here.
 */

import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Skill Changes Per Class (v83 to CoT 2) - Liven's Classic Maple Guide"
	description="Which first-job skills survived v83 into MapleStory Classic World, which got dropped, and which are brand new. Confirmed changes: Warrior gained Precise Strikes, Bowman lost Blessing of Amazon and gained Power Knockback. Magician and Thief kits are unchanged."
	currentPath="/guides"
	theme="perion"
	decorations={false}
>
	<section class="section-heading">
		<div>
			<span class="eyebrow eyebrow--guide">CoT 2 vs v83 Reality Check</span>
			<h1>Skill Changes Per Class</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Every returning player's build plan starts from muscle memory:
				"max Power Strike, then Slash Blast, then Iron Body." Some of
				that advice still works. Some of it needs a footnote. Two
				classes have confirmed kit changes in CoT 2; two are unchanged
				from v83. Here's the class-by-class rundown, all datamine-verified.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<article class="prose">
		<div class="callout callout--framing">
			<strong>Verification:</strong> the skill LISTS and skill IDs below
			are 100% CoT 2-verified against ohmi69's client-datamine
			dashboard at
			<a href="https://osmsdataexplorer.com" rel="external nofollow">osmsdataexplorer.com</a>.
			Damage percentages, max-level values, and MP costs still reflect
			v83-era baseline - Nexon may have retuned individual skill numbers
			without us noticing yet. Once Founder's Access opens October 6,
			numeric values get live-verified.
		</div>

		<h2 id="summary">The 30-second summary</h2>
		<div class="guide-summary-grid">
			<div class="guide-summary-card guide-summary-card--changed">
				<h3>Warrior <span class="status-pill status-pill--new">+1 SKILL</span></h3>
				<p>
					Gained a new 6th passive: <strong>Precise Strikes</strong>
					(accuracy + crit rate). Other 5 skills unchanged.
					Standard v83 build order still valid, just slot the new
					skill for utility.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="guide-summary-card guide-summary-card--changed">
				<h3>Bowman <span class="status-pill status-pill--rework">SKILL SWAP</span></h3>
				<p>
					Lost <strong>Blessing of Amazon</strong> (the classic party
					attack buff), gained <strong>Power Knockback</strong>
					(CC AoE that always crits). Significant build rethink.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="guide-summary-card guide-summary-card--same">
				<h3>Magician <span class="status-pill status-pill--same">UNCHANGED</span></h3>
				<p>
					All six first-job skills match v83 baseline exactly. Your
					old build plan works as-is.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="guide-summary-card guide-summary-card--same">
				<h3>Thief <span class="status-pill status-pill--same">UNCHANGED</span></h3>
				<p>
					All six first-job skills match v83 baseline exactly. The
					datamine calls it "Rogue" internally but the visible class
					name is unchanged. Same DEX-for-advancement quirk, same
					Lucky Seven, same Bandit Steal.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2 id="warrior">Warrior: gained Precise Strikes</h2>
		<p>
			The classic v83 Warrior 1st-job kit had five skills: Improved HP
			Recovery, Improved MaxHP Increase, Power Strike, Slash Blast, and
			Iron Body. CoT 2 keeps all five with unchanged names/IDs and adds
			a sixth:
		</p>

		<div class="skill-callout skill-callout--new">
			<div class="skill-callout__head">
				<span class="skill-callout__badge">NEW IN COT 2</span>
				<h3>Precise Strikes</h3>
				<span class="skill-callout__meta">Passive &middot; Max Lv 15 &middot; Skill ID 1000002</span>
			</div>
			<p>
				Repeated practice with your weapon increases <strong>Accuracy
				and Critical Rate</strong>. A passive quality-of-life boost -
				Accuracy helps you actually connect with same-level or
				higher-level mobs, and Crit is genuinely rare on Warriors, so
				this fills two subtle-but-real gaps.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Suggested allocation:</strong> 1 point utility, or
				fully skip in favor of the classic v83 damage-first build.
				With only 61 SP total available across levels 10-30 and five
				core skills competing for them, Precise Strikes isn't a
				priority for grinders. Boss-focused Warriors might invest more
				for the accuracy floor.
			</p>
		</div>

		<p>
			<strong>Revised recommended order (Warrior):</strong>
			1 point in Improved HP Recovery, then max Improved MaxHP Increase
			(compounds every level), then max Power Strike, then max Slash
			Blast, then Iron Body with anything left over. Slot Precise
			Strikes at 1-point utility once you're at 30, or skip it entirely
			if you're comfortable with the classic build.
		</p>
		<p>
			See <a href="/jobs/warrior">the full Warrior guide</a> for the
			complete 1st-job skill breakdown with numbers.
		</p>

		<h2 id="bowman">Bowman: lost Blessing of Amazon, gained Power Knockback</h2>
		<p>
			The <strong>biggest single class change confirmed in CoT 2.</strong>
			The classic v83 Bowman 1st-job kit had six skills: Blessing of
			Amazon (party attack buff), Critical Shot, the Booster
			(Hunter's Focus / Crossbow Focus), the Soul Arrow variant,
			Arrow Blow, and Double Shot. CoT 2 dropped Blessing of Amazon
			entirely and replaced it with:
		</p>

		<div class="skill-callout skill-callout--rework">
			<div class="skill-callout__head">
				<span class="skill-callout__badge skill-callout__badge--rework">REPLACES BLESSING OF AMAZON</span>
				<h3>Power Knockback</h3>
				<span class="skill-callout__meta">Attack &middot; Max Lv 15 &middot; CoT 2 verified</span>
			</div>
			<p>
				Swings the bow widely to push multiple enemies far back.
				<strong>This attack ALWAYS crits</strong>, and higher skill
				levels increase the number of mobs pushed per swing. A
				genuine mob-training utility, especially on maps where
				kite-and-shoot beats stand-and-deliver.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Why this matters for returners:</strong> Blessing of
				Amazon was a party utility that many v83 builds threw a few
				points into for the group buff. Power Knockback is a
				completely different mechanic - a solo-mobility crowd
				control attack, not a party buff. If your v83 memory tells
				you "throw 3 points into Amazon for the party synergy",
				forget that entirely.
			</p>
		</div>

		<p>
			<strong>Revised recommended order (Bowman):</strong>
			1 point in Arrow Blow so you have an attack, then MAX Double Shot
			(pure damage winner), then MAX Critical Shot (damage multiplier),
			then evaluate Power Knockback based on your training style -
			grinders love it, boss-focused Bowmen skip it for the Booster.
			Blessing of Amazon is gone; do not budget SP for it.
		</p>
		<p>
			See <a href="/jobs/bowman">the full Bowman guide</a> for the
			complete 1st-job skill breakdown with numbers.
		</p>

		<h2 id="magician">Magician: no changes, use v83 build as-is</h2>
		<p>
			All six first-job Magician skills match the v83 baseline exactly:
			Improved MP Recovery, Improved MaxMP Increase, Magic Guard, Magic
			Armor, Energy Bolt, Magic Claw. Same skill IDs, same names, same
			mechanics per the datamine.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Recommended order (unchanged from v83):</strong>
			1 point in Energy Bolt for an attack, max Magic Claw (your
			workhorse), max Magic Guard (the survival skill that defines
			Magicians), then MP Recovery + MaxMP as SP allows. Magic Armor
			is optional utility.
		</p>
		<p>
			Numeric values (MP costs, Magic Guard's damage-to-MP ratio,
			advancement level) still reflect v83 baseline pending live
			confirmation. See <a href="/jobs/magician">the full Magician
			guide</a>.
		</p>

		<h2 id="thief">Thief: no changes, still called "Rogue" in the datamine</h2>
		<p>
			All six first-job Thief skills match v83 baseline. Nimble Feet,
			Keen Eyes, Disorder, Dark Sight, Lucky Seven, and Double Stab
			all present with unchanged IDs. Datamine files call the class
			"Rogue" internally (Nexon's canonical class name for the 1st job
			tier) but the visible in-game name is unchanged.
		</p>
		<p>
			Class quirks preserved from v83:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Advancement requires DEX 25</strong>, not the STR/DEX/
				etc. minimum other classes use. New players sometimes miss
				this and get stuck at Lv 10 with wrong AP.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Lucky Seven damage formula is LUK-only</strong>, not
				LUK+DEX. Foundational to the Assassin build later; overinvest
				LUK from Lv 1.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Bandit Steal drop rates unchanged</strong> (per the
				datamine skill definition). Assassin vs Bandit is still the
				same fork at Lv 30.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			See <a href="/jobs/thief">the full Thief guide</a>.
		</p>

		<h2 id="second-job">What about 2nd + 3rd job?</h2>
		<p>
			We've only surfaced <strong>1st-job</strong> skill changes so far.
			2nd-job class splits (Fighter/Page/Spearman, Hunter/Crossbowman,
			Wizard-FP/Wizard-IL/Cleric, Assassin/Bandit) exist in the
			datamine but we haven't done the full v83-vs-CoT2 diff on those
			kits yet. The Sprint plan is to do the 2nd job pass once
			Founder's Access opens, so we can validate against live behavior
			at the same time.
		</p>
		<p>
			If a 2nd job skill on the class page you're reading has a
			<code>verificationStatus: "closed-test-info"</code> tag, treat
			the numeric values as v83-baseline until noted otherwise.
		</p>

		<h2 id="how-to-check">How to check a specific skill</h2>
		<p>
			The class-specific job pages are the authoritative source:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li><a href="/jobs/warrior">Warrior</a> - full skill breakdown with numbers</li>
			<li><a href="/jobs/magician">Magician</a></li>
			<li><a href="/jobs/bowman">Bowman</a></li>
			<li><a href="/jobs/thief">Thief</a></li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Each page lists every skill in the 1st-job kit with its skill ID,
			max level, mechanic summary, and suggested AP allocation. Skills
			flagged "New in CoT 2" or "CoT 2 verified" are datamine-confirmed;
			everything else uses v83 baseline values that we'll re-verify
			post-launch.
		</p>

		<h2 id="next-2nd-job">What about 2nd job?</h2>
		<p>
			1st-job kits are datamine-confirmed. 2nd-job kits are canonical
			v83 pending Founder's Access verification. If you're planning
			ahead for your Lv 30 branch decision, we've got a dedicated
			guide per class:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li><a href="/guides/warrior-2nd-job">Warrior: Fighter, Page, or Spearman?</a> - three-branch decision, all skill kits and build orders.</li>
			<li><a href="/guides/magician-2nd-job">Magician: F/P, I/L, or Cleric?</a> - element choice + Cleric heal-farming.</li>
			<li><a href="/guides/bowman-2nd-job">Bowman: Hunter or Crossbowman?</a> - covers the Power Knockback shuffle specific to this branch.</li>
			<li><a href="/guides/thief-2nd-job">Thief: Assassin or Bandit?</a> - ranged stars vs melee daggers.</li>
		</ul>

		<p class="closing">
			Related: <a href="/guides/whats-new-in-cot2">What's New in CoT 2</a>
			for the broader zone-and-systems changelog, and
			<a href="/guides/exp-then-vs-now">Then vs Now: EXP &amp;
			Progression</a> for how mob/quest EXP values changed alongside
			the skill kits.
		</p>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.section-heading {
		max-width: 68ch;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}
	.lede {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		color: var(--text-body);
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		line-height: 1.55;
	}

	.prose {
		max-width: 76ch;
		font-size: 1rem;
		line-height: 1.62;
		color: var(--text-body);
	}
	.prose h2 {
		margin-top: 2.2rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--text-heading);
		font-size: 1.5rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-card);
		padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
	}
	.prose h3 {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--text-heading);
		font-size: 1.15rem;
	}
	.prose p,
	.prose ul,
	.prose ol {
		margin-top: 0.7rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
	}
	.prose li {
		margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
	}
	.prose code {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.88em;
		background: var(--bg-cloud);
		padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
		border-radius: 0.25rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border-card);
	}
	.prose a {
		color: var(--accent-primary);
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-decoration-thickness: 0.09em;
		text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
	}
	.prose strong {
		color: var(--text-heading);
	}
	.prose .closing {
		margin-top: 2.2rem;
		padding-top: 1rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border-card);
		font-style: italic;
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}

	.callout {
		margin: 1.2rem 0;
		padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border-card);
		background: var(--bg-cloud);
		border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-primary);
	}

	.skill-callout {
		margin: 1.2rem 0;
		padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
		background: var(--surface-card);
		border: 1px solid var(--border-card);
		border-radius: 0.55rem;
	}
	.skill-callout--new { border-left: 4px solid #158a4d; }
	.skill-callout--rework { border-left: 4px solid #b8730e; }
	.skill-callout__head {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		align-items: baseline;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	.skill-callout__badge {
		/* Sprint 67 typography floor: bumped from 0.65 -> 0.78. */
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		font-weight: 800;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		padding: 0.15rem 0.45rem;
		background: #158a4d;
		color: white;
		border-radius: 999px;
	}
	.skill-callout__badge--rework { background: #b8730e; }
	.skill-callout h3 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		color: var(--text-heading);
		border: none;
		padding: 0;
		flex: 1 1 auto;
	}
	.skill-callout__meta {
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
	}
	.skill-callout p {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
</style>
